1
00:06:17,647 --> 00:06:23,647
Miss World 1970: The launch of a revolution

2
00:12:35,294 --> 00:12:41,294
Misbehaviour is a drama, history, comedy film directed by Philippa Lowthorpe.

3
00:18:52,941 --> 00:18:58,941
A group of women involved in the Women's Liberation Movement hatched a plan to invade the stage and disrupt the live broadcast
at the 1970 Miss World competition in London, resulting in overnight fame for the newly-formed organization.

4
00:25:10,588 --> 00:25:16,588
When the show resumed, the results caused an uproar and
turned the Western ideal of beauty on its head.

5
00:31:28,235 --> 00:31:34,235
Sally Alexander, played by Keira Knightley.

6
00:37:45,882 --> 00:37:51,882
Jennifer Hosten - Miss Grenada, played by Gugu Mbatha-Raw.

7
00:44:03,529 --> 00:44:09,529
Jo Robinson, played by Jessie Buckley.

8
00:50:21,176 --> 00:50:27,176
Julia Morley, played by Keeley Hawes.

9
00:56:38,823 --> 00:56:44,823
Evelyn Alexander, played by Phyllis Logan.

10
01:02:56,470 --> 01:03:02,470
Dolores Hope, played by Lesley Manville.

11
01:09:14,117 --> 01:09:20,117
Misbehaviour is a 2020 British comedy-drama film directed by Philippa Lowthorpe, from a
screenplay by Gaby Chiappe and Rebecca Frayn, from a story by Frayn.

12
01:15:31,764 --> 01:15:37,764
The film stars Keira Knightley, Gugu Mbatha-Raw, Jessie Buckley, Keeley Hawes,
Phyllis Logan, Lesley Manville, Rhys Ifans and Greg Kinnear.

13
01:21:49,411 --> 01:21:55,411
Misbehaviour was released in the United Kingdom on 13 March 2020 by Pathé's distribution
partner Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures through 20th Century Fox.

14
01:28:07,058 --> 01:28:13,058
It is the final film from Pathé UK to be released
under the 20th Century Fox name.

15
01:34:24,705 --> 01:34:30,705
The film explores themes of london, england, 1970s,
commune, affectation, beauty contest.

16
01:40:42,352 --> 01:40:48,352
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
